      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did uppu mean, and what did puttakam mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கண்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கண் (kaṇ) — \"an eye\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian kaṇ, held almost still everywhere it went: Malayalam കണ്ണ്, Telugu కన్ను, Kannada ಕಣ್ಣು. Tamil's is the shortest of the four, one syllable and done."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It reaches well past the face. A kaṇ is the joint on a stalk of sugarcane and the mesh of a net — wherever a thing has an opening or a knot, Tamil is willing to call it an eye."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "talai and kai, the head and the hand, came earlier. The face gets its own turn now, one piece at a time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five more parts of the body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kaṇ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kaṇ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kaṇ, then talai, so the part and the whole sit together",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kaṇ*, then *talai*, so the part and the whole sit together]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does கண் (kaṇ) mean? (\"an eye\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
