        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: காது",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "காது (kādu) — \"an ear\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here it is Tamil that stands apart. kādu is the ear a Tamil speaker has, and the other three sisters built their everyday word on a different root altogether: Malayalam ചെവി, Telugu చెవి, Kannada ಕಿವಿ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tamil owns that root as well. செவி (sevi) names the same organ and is kept for poetry and formal speech — so the word the sisters use over breakfast is the one Tamil holds back for its high register. Two words, one ear, and the occasion decides which."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: an eye and an ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
