              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மூக்கு (mūkku) — \"a nose\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Another word the family barely touched: Malayalam മൂക്ക്, Telugu ముక్కు, Kannada ಮೂಗು. Only the ending moves."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mūkku also names the point of a thing — the prow of a boat, the tip of a pen. Whatever sticks out in front is the nose of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and all three are on the face."
            }
