        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பல்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பல் (pal) — \"a tooth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian pal, and the sisters pulled it three ways. Malayalam പല്ല്, Kannada ಹಲ್ಲು, Telugu పన్ను. Kannada is the odd one again, with the same p- to h- shift the fruit-word showed; Telugu turned the l into an n. Tamil stops the word dead on its l and adds nothing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In everyday speech it often comes out pallu, with the l doubled — which is exactly the shape Malayalam and Kannada put on the page."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and the first one you can bite with."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
