        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: வயிறு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "வயிறு (vayiṟu) — \"the stomach\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ற in the middle is the hard ṟ this book met at aṟai, 'a room' — not the soft r of peyar. Malayalam says വയറ്, the same word; Telugu and Kannada went elsewhere entirely for this one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where an English speaker says they are hungry, Tamil is happy to talk about the vayiṟu and leave the person out of it: the belly is what is empty, and you merely own it. That is the same habit behind uṅgaḷ uḍambu eppaḍi irukku, where the health question hangs on the body rather than on you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That closes the run: an eye, an ear, a nose, a tooth, and what holds the food."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
